# Testing

## Locations

- Unit and ViewModel tests: `app/src/test/java/com/noshitechinc/restaurant/`, mirroring the main package.
- Compose UI tests: `app/src/androidTest/java/com/noshitechinc/restaurant/`.
- Fakes: `app/src/test/java/com/noshitechinc/restaurant/fakes/` (`FakeXxx`).
- Shared rules: `app/src/test/java/com/noshitechinc/restaurant/testing/` (`MainDispatcherRule`).

## Libraries

- JUnit4 with `kotlin.test` assertions, MockK, Turbine and kotlinx-coroutines-test (`runTest`).
- Prefer fakes over mocks for repositories and core interfaces; use MockK for leaf collaborators or interaction checks.
- Test flows with Turbine: `flow.test { awaitItem() }`.
- Never use `Thread.sleep` or `runBlocking`; control time with the test dispatcher.

## ViewModels

- Add `@get:Rule val mainDispatcherRule = MainDispatcherRule()` to every ViewModel test.
- Model new ViewModel tests on `HomeViewModelTest`.
- Cover `LoadState` transitions, effects (`ShowMessage`, `ShowErrorDialog`, feature effects) and `launchSubmit` duplicate-tap protection via `submittingKeys`.

## Networking

- Test OkHttp interceptors, `TokenAuthenticator` and Retrofit services with MockWebServer; never hit a real network.

## Compose UI

- Use `createComposeRule()` and wrap content in `AppTheme { }`.
- Find nodes by test tag (`Modifier.testTag`, tag objects such as `StateTags`), not by display text.

## Naming and commands

- Name unit tests in `app/src/test` as backticked sentences: ``fun `does X when Y`()``.
- Name instrumented tests in `app/src/androidTest` in camelCase (`fun doesXWhenY()`): method names with spaces fail D8 below API 30 and `minSdk` is 25.
- Run `./gradlew testDevDebugUnitTest` for unit tests and `./gradlew connectedDevDebugAndroidTest` for UI tests (prefix `ANDROID_HOME=$HOME/Android/Sdk`).
